Z||000007||Shaft||11-21-2000||08:02 PM||||Actually the DeLorian (sp?) was first seen by car magazines in 1979. Of course John Delorian used to be a Pontiac designer before venturing out on his own. I think Pontiac didn't like John leaving and designed a car along the same lines as his. And since GM had more resources they could sell more and effectively put John DeLorian out of business.<P>Just my $.02||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||11-21-2000||10:40 PM||||I cannot speak for them all, but I am going to need an explanation on how Probe's look like Fiero's.  I have owned both body styles (first gen and second gen) of Probes and never really thought they were stylistic ripoff's of the Fiero styling.  <P>Ok, I know that the Fiero GT's are fastbacks which is similar to the Probe's hatchback.  But profile views of the two do not look very similar.  From the front the 1 gen Probes are much more substantial with their grille.  The second gen's look less like Fiero's.  No belt line around the car, curves and contours down the sides instead of how the Fiero's is kinda like a parenthasis ( .  They both have pop-up lights<P>Please don't feel flamed.  I hope I haven't sounded angry or offended.  I think the Fiero's look better than the Probes.  More sporty!  But I just cannot see the connection.  <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/Probe07.JPG">  <BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<P>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 11-21-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||11-22-2000||09:35 AM||||How are Del Sols wannabe Fiero's?  I think the only thing they have in common is 2 seats and 4 wheels.  The Del Sol vtec is a pretty quick, but other then that they are about as fast as bone stock V6s, maybe a little slower.  If anything, most newer 2 seaters are Miata wannabe's...<P>I think that Suzuki XT6, XTC (or something like that) is a Fiero clone (body wise).  <P>If you see a Ford Probe from a distance while you are headed up one side of the road and they are coming down the other, it looks like an MR2.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 11-22-2000).]||||reg||1
